{%- comment -%}
  Product aggregateRating JSON-LD — sourced from the Judge.me review metafield, the same
  source this theme's own snippets/reviews-star-rating.liquid already reads from
  (product.metafields.judgeme.review_widget_data). Emitted ONLY when a product has at least
  one real review — Google requires reviewCount > 0, and an empty/fabricated rating is worse
  than none.
  DATA CHECK 2026-08-07 (debug: currently forced on to verify parsing — see TEMP-DEBUG below):
  sampled 8 live products spanning publish dates back to Dec 2024 — all show 0 accumulated
  Judge.me reviews, metafield last synced 2026-08-06 (same timestamp on every product, i.e.
  a full fresh sync, not gradual accumulation). This contradicts the Product SEO Audit
  (2026-08-06)'s assumption that reviews already existed — flagging as an open discrepancy,
  not silently resolving it. The "52+ reviews" homepage copy is Google Business Profile
  reviews (a different entity, already schema'd on the homepage), not Shopify product reviews.
  Added 2026-08-07.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if template contains 'product' -%}
  {%- assign review_data = product.metafields.judgeme.review_widget_data.value -%}
  {%- comment -%} TEMP-DEBUG: forcing render regardless of review count, to verify the metafield parses correctly given every sampled product currently has 0 reviews. Will be reverted to the real `review_data.number_of_reviews > 0` guard before this is considered done. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if review_data -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json" id="schema-product-rating-debug">
  {
    "DEBUG_number_of_reviews": {{ review_data.number_of_reviews | json }},
    "DEBUG_average_rating": {{ review_data.average_rating | json }}
  }
  </script>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
